  <div class="post-featured-img"><img src="/assets/img-19-1.webp" alt="Tax Credits and Deductions That Are Often Overlooked" loading="lazy"/></div>
  <div class="post-content"><p>Taking advantage of tax credits and deductions is the easiest way to lower your tax bill. Below is a list of commonly overlooked options that could save you money.</p><h2>For Homeowners</h2><ul><li><strong>Selling Costs Deduction:</strong> When you sell your home for profit, selling costs are deductible</li><li><strong>Mortgage Interest:</strong> Deductible for homes up to $750,000</li><li><strong>Property Tax:</strong> State and local property taxes up to $10,000</li></ul><h2>For Parents</h2><ul><li><strong>Child Tax Credit:</strong> Up to $2,000 per qualifying child</li><li><strong>Child and Dependent Care Credit:</strong> For daycare and childcare expenses</li><li><strong>Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC):</strong> For low to moderate income earners</li></ul><h2>For Self-Employed / Business Owners</h2><ul><li>Home office deduction</li><li>Vehicle mileage deduction</li><li>Self-employed health insurance</li><li>Retirement plan contributions (SEP IRA, SIMPLE IRA)</li></ul><a href="/en/consultation" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:8px;">Schedule a Consultation</a></div>
